  1920   0    994 |    0.1642     0.2348     0.3163 |    0.1647    0.2341    0.3140

Interpretation: if |S(at)|/t and |nu_hat(a)| CONVERGE to fixed constants
(t-independent), the self-similarity is a SCALING LAW terminating at the
fixed 7-comb nu_hat -- ONE step, NOT a tower.  Error -> c* = |nu_hat(1)| fixed.
A genuine recursion would instead give a SHRINKING sequence with no fixed base.

